(R/'FROZEN_LOSS_SPECIFICATION.md').write_text(r'''# Sealed mask-aware initialization objective

Only the independent low-level actor is optimized. J1 remains eval/no_grad and outside every optimizer. Critics, planner, reachability and target networks are frozen. The actor is newly initialized with zero residual output layers, so it initially reproduces J1; no V2 tiny-adapter or untrained engineering-fixture weights initialize this scientific lineage.

Each update accumulates literal independent-prefix microbatches of one, then makes exactly one AdamW actor step. Define A as ordinary next-AA cross entropy; G as negative physical distance/angle/torsion log density summed over valid components and divided by that decision's contributing component count; K_A as exact categorical KL(adapted||frozen J1); K_G as AA-policy-weighted conditional latent Gaussian KL, divided by valid component count. The shared, bijective exp / pi*sigmoid / pi*tanh transformations make latent Gaussian KL equal physical KL on the same component support. Density likelihood retains all original Jacobians and physical units. Missing components contribute neither likelihood nor geometric KL. No geometric label is invented.

The exact objective is:

L = mean_64[A + .05 G + .02 K_A + .01 K_G]
  + mean_32[.10 G + .01 K_G]
  + .25 mean_8[A + .10 G + .02 K_A + .01 K_G + .05 H].

The first stream uses 40/30/30 complete/partial-only/AA-only decisions. Partial components are admitted only where observed mapped anchors and continuity satisfy existing component masks. AA-only has G=K_G=0. The second is independent, complete, identity-first geometry supervision; its true selected AA conditions the geometry head but has no CE term. All terms are averaged within their stream before applying stream weights. Microbatch=1 is sealed: zero-mask rows contribute zero rather than changing any other row's normalization. Stream coefficients are prospective choices, not validation-tuned optima or a claim of TRAIN gradient-scale optimality. This differs from the prior generic launcher: it makes the goal stream's AA weight explicitly .25, avoids an extra AA KL on the geometry-only stream, and uses valid partial local geometry at .05.

H is only a one-step explicit-target guide. At a task target whose index is exactly the next residue, construct the next C-alpha from the deterministic transformed latent mean (a representative, NOT the physical predictive mean). Use squared target-position error d²/(64+d²). If a target orientation exists, add .5*(3-tr(R_pred R_goal^T))/4, clamped to [0,1]. Thus 0<=H<=1.5 and its maximum whole-objective contribution is .01875. All required prefix anchors must be genuinely available and all action components valid. Other timesteps contribute zero H; there are no gradients through an ungenerated suffix. NLL still fits means and uncertainty; this guide does not replace calibrated likelihood.

P0 has sequence constraints and backbone validity, P1 additionally has the native endpoint position, P2 midpoint and endpoint positions/orientations. Frames use the preserved right-handed initial-three-anchor gauge. Native targets are sparse public task instructions, not a hidden full-backbone input. Goal demonstrations teach canonical AA and valid local geometry under these public goals. Trivial motif copying is reported separately from unconstrained next-AA performance; goal sensitivity alone is not success or causal planning.

AA mix prefixes are sampled over true canonical positions 0..N-1. Complete geometry components are valid only for t>=1/2/3; partial masks additionally require real observed anchors and valid continuity. No AA targets are deleted because geometry is absent. Missing coordinates are masked independently from known sequence tokens. No future native AA suffix or undisclosed future coordinate reaches prepare()/J1/the independent actor.

The launcher's admission-specific stream_weights are authoritative; the inherited generic loss_weights and SAC-only fields are dormant in this stage. Fresh actor-only AdamW: weight decay .01, peak LR 5e-5, 250-update linear warmup from 2e-7, cosine decay to 5e-6 at update 10000, total actor gradient norm clip1. BF16 neural forward, FP32 optimizer, original appropriate FP32/FP64 geometric density and C-alpha construction. Frozen J1 is always eval; the independent actor uses its original V3 architecture with SDPA dropout0, not a new pretrained J1 dropout setting. Inactive optimizers are absent, so they cannot silently receive weight decay or moments.

Log each normalized component and stream contribution, valid component counts, encoder/AA/geometry gradient norms and total clipping norm. At scheduled evaluations, a fixed TRAIN-only prefix compares shared-encoder gradients of AA CE and local geometry+goal guidance using autograd.grad without optimizer steps. Zero encoder gradients at residual initialization are explicitly undefined cosine, not fabricated agreement. Coefficients remain fixed throughout this lineage. Instability/conflict stopping is in the sampling and validation protocol.
''')
(R/'SAMPLING_AND_CURRICULUM_PROTOCOL.md').write_text('''# Frozen sampling and curriculum

No new scientific split. Accepted E016 TRAIN: complete21475, partial-only29129, AA-only67615, total118219. Complete63315 qualified observations and partial118461 observations are source inventories; the latter includes complete-view overlap and is NOT a disjoint identity count. Partial-only excludes complete identities. All AA-only coordinates remain withheld. Original source manifests, mapping/continuity masks and deposited lengths stay authoritative.

Per update:64 primary AA decisions,32 additional complete geometry decisions,8 goal-conditioned complete demonstrations. A persistent ten-slot cycle gives4/3/3 AA decisions; five64-decision updates realize128/96/96 exactly. Identity sweeps are independently shuffled within population before repeat; each identity has its own shuffled position-coverage cycle. A uniform qualified observation is chosen after identity selection. Complete-geometry sampling has independent coverage/RNG. Goals use a separate TRAIN-only complete-identity sweep with uniform observation choice and native-validity rejection; category cycle is P0/P1/P2, never random outcome-based category selection.

Goals: updates1–2500 use lengths64–96 (2659 candidate identities);2501–5000 use64–128 (6890);5001–10000 use64–256 (14804). Each expanded pool starts a documented new shuffled sweep; its cursor persists thereafter. These are metadata candidates, not a claim all observations pass the old native-validity envelope. At most64 rejected draws per requested valid goal before a hard diagnostic stop. Record skipped identities/observations, rejection counts and actual exposure; no source record is removed or relabelled. Goal position sampling alternates a uniform constrained motif/geometric-target position with a uniform broad prefix in3..N-1. Goal categories balance across calls, not per eight-example batch. Goal construction and observation choice use independent seed1705; AA1703; geometry1704. There is no generated-prefix supervision or high-level correction optimization in this stage.

Over10k updates if uninterrupted:640000 primary AA decisions (256000/192000/192000),320000 additional complete geometry decisions,80000 goal-conditioned AA+geometry demonstrations (P0/P1/P2 =26667/26667/26666). Thus720000 CE decisions; the geometry-only stream uses selected AA as conditioning, not another320000 CE labels. Analytical expectation over uniform identity/observation/position selection is approximately827688 distance,821017 angle and814346 torsion targets over10k across all streams (EXPECTED_GEOMETRY_TARGET_COUNTS.json); actual deterministic counts are logged. Goal demonstrations supply240000 component targets; complete geometry adds at most960000, with positions0..2 removing undefined components. Primary AA stream actual valid geometry counts depend on sampled observation masks/positions; report measured values, never assume all64 have three targets. Effective objective stream weights are in FROZEN_LOSS_SPECIFICATION.md, not proportional to stream sample counts.

The metadata-only sampler simulation encountered all118219 identities by5000 updates and640000 distinct primary identity-position labels by10000, zero repeats. By2500 it covered21475 complete,29129 partial-only and48000 AA-only identities. This is a discarded scheduling simulation, NOT training exposure. Observation-selection RNG consumption can change the exact future identity/position ordering after sweeps; the sweep counts and no-position-repeat guarantees remain. Actual counts from the training samplers are authoritative. Goal native-validity rejection makes exact future unique goal coverage unknowable a priori. Long lengths257–500 are trained by AA/complete geometry auxiliaries but remain goal-generalization stress tests.

VALIDATION:144 identities, eight per six length bands20–63/64–96/97–128/129–256/257–384/385–500 and three disjoint populations. Each has four fixed prefix positions, yielding576 decisions per native/missing-geometry condition.120 sparse P0/P1/P2 tasks on40 complete identities >=64 have438 goal-conditioned prefix decisions. TRAIN diagnostics use independently hash-selected144 TRAIN identities,576 paired-condition decisions and437 task decisions. No identity or protected homology-group overlap. Manifest references contain source IDs/hashes and selected observations; no raw dataset duplication.

Selection:seed1729 SHA256 identity ranking within each predefined cell before prediction; no selection based on model scores or native witness validity. Equal length-band/population/identity weighting defines the primary balanced geometry-free AA retention metric. This deliberately balanced panel is not an estimate of unweighted whole-population E016 perplexity. All target positions within identity are averaged first. Report native/geometry-free metrics, category/length/relative-position strata, top1/top3 and individual distance/angle/torsion NLL. Tasks use equal band/category/identity weights. Paired2000-replicate identity bootstrap within strata reports NLL changes from +0; exact identities are not independent evolutionary families. Small cell sizes limit inference.

Native-witness audit retained one VALIDATION and two TRAIN identity stress cases that fail older short-domain backbone calibration (three tasks per identity). These are flagged, not silently excluded or used to retune limits. P0/P1/P2 task scores stratify native-witness validity. Native geometric goals are constructible by their actual coordinates, but strict joint validity may be impossible for flagged tasks; do not count their failure as an actor's inability to reproduce a feasible jointly valid target. The old envelope remains fixed; broader calibration would be a separate TRAIN-only scientific decision.

Free generation:60 frozen VALIDATION task/seed attempts (two complete identities per five >=64 length bands × three categories × two seeds). Core12 attempts covers64–128; standard30 covers all bands; extended60 adds second identities. +0/+250 use core; +1000/+2500/+5000 standard; +10000 extended. Compare frozen J1 on identical task/anchor/seed/FP64 noise conditions; cache only exact protocol/tier/reference matches. No failure replacement, no planner/rewind, no native hidden suffix, no external oracle. Report completion, exact motif and pose success, finite/valid backbones, clashes, compactness, contacts, adjacent geometry, torsion/angle distributions, exact sequence duplicates/composition; these are geometric task proxies, not biological stability. Fixed source initial three native anchors are declared context, not de novo whole-chain folding evidence.

Evaluate at+0 before the first optimizer update and+250,+1000,+2500,+5000,+10000. Two successive scheduled evaluations trigger stop for balanced geometry-free or native AA regression >.05nats from+0; matched gap growth >.10nats with no held-out AA gain; task supervised objective regression >.10; or any component NLL degradation >.20nats. Negative TRAIN encoder AA-vs-geometry/goal cosine<-.5 together with held-out AA regression>.025nats also requires two successive evaluations. Cosine alone does not certify conflict and does not stop. Stop for free-generation completion<90%, or zero valid generated backbones at/after2500; report finite small-sample limitations. At/after5000 stop for <.005nats geometry-free AA AND <.01 task-objective improvement since2500. No automatic extension beyond10000. Nonfinite loss/gradients, changed frozen tensors or unrecoverable resource pressure stop immediately while preserving latest durable recovery. Storage pause is not scientific failure. Latest/best retention does not automatically promote a scientifically acceptable generator.
''')
(R/'TRAINING_READINESS_REPORT.md').write_text(f'''# E017 V3 supervised-initialization admission

**Engineering/storage ready; training not started and awaits approval.** Source `{commit}`, branch `{branch}`, derived from verified4374c4a. All historical releases remain unchanged. No optimizer updates, no J1 updates, no TEST scoring, no production RL, no new external inference.

Frozen J1 checkpoint `{MAIN}`, SHA256 `{SHA}` verifies before load. Its12,351,746 parameters/buffers stayed bitwise identical in the bounded GPU checks. The independent system retains **63,389,056** parameter capacity and36,235,748 target-copy parameters. This stage updates **only17,438,114 low-level actor parameters**;45,950,942 other independent parameters, all targets and J1 stay frozen. Only the actor belongs to an optimizer. Complete recovery still contains all networks/targets, actor AdamW/scheduler, independent samplers, RNG, counters/monitor, configuration/source/data identities and replay binding. Inactive components have no optimizer state to invent or allocate. Original V3 architecture/capacity is not reduced.

The frozen VALIDATION panel has144 identities/576 paired-condition prefix decisions,120 P0/P1/P2 tasks/438 task-prefix decisions, and60 frozen generation attempts. Matched TRAIN diagnostics are separate; zero cross-partition identity/protected-group overlap. Controls include native and fully missing geometry, goal-on vs goal-off distribution sensitivity and stratified direct free generation. Five goal length bands64–500 plus short20–63 AA controls are covered. All panels were selected before scoring. No full panel or free-generation campaign ran here; nine small fixture decisions and one next-action construction exercised the implementation only. Native witness out-of-envelope cases remain flagged. See [panels](panels/FROZEN_VALIDATION_MANIFEST.json), [sampling](SAMPLING_AND_CURRICULUM_PROTOCOL.md), [loss](FROZEN_LOSS_SPECIFICATION.md).

Prospective ceiling10000 updates, validation at250/1000/2500/5000/10000 plus+0. LR warmup250, peak5e-5, cosine floor5e-6, microbatch1, gradient clip1. Primary AA64 uses40/30/30; independent32 complete geometry plus8 native goal demonstrations. Goal classes are balanced from the outset, curriculum64–96 then128 then256; longer goal tasks are explicitly held-out stress strata. No critic/planner/reachability learning. Losses and scientific stop rules are sealed before validation; no weight search or validation fitting.

Zero-update preflight passed: authoritative membership/split checks, quota/coverage simulation, AA/goal sampler exact restoration, masked-geometry finiteness/placeholder invariance, no geometric loss from AA-only, complete recovery readback and exact CPU/CUDA/Python/numpy RNG restoration. The full recovery fixture is a19.65MB development engineering checkpoint, not trained evidence. Research architecture serialization was measured to a counting stream; no redundant ~600MB untrained checkpoint was left on D:. Prior storage-release files were checksum-verified. Original research backward/restart engineering evidence is reused, not rerun as a training experiment. Read [preflight](results/BOUNDED_ADMISSION_PREFLIGHT.json) and [final protocol checks](results/FINAL_PROTOCOL_CHECKS.json).

Storage:current D:free **{free/gib:.2f}GiB**; stage-specific complete checkpoint **{tests['full_scope_actor_Adam_checkpoint_bytes']/2**20:.1f}MiB**, full-coverage scenario **{C/2**20:.1f}MiB**. Latest+distinct best persist at{2*C/gib:.2f}GiB; peak with one incoming atomic checkpoint{3*C/gib:.2f}GiB. Including2GiB headroom and96MiB forecast outputs requires{resource['required_conservative_free_bytes']/gib:.2f}GiB now. The700MiB startup hint is conservative; each actual write is measured and readback verified. Warnings near4GiB; pre-update/next-write admission pauses if future complete write cannot fit with2GiB headroom. Empty initialization replay reuses its immutable snapshot. Never retire historical files, certified data or anything outside a newly owned run.

Save once after+0 scoring before any update, then every250 updates OR1800seconds at an update boundary, every evaluation and final/early-stop boundary. Do not write both periodic and evaluation checkpoints for the same update. Retain only latest/best verified complete recovery, with temporary atomic staging; best uses balanced geometry-free validation AA NLL as a retention ranking, not joint-quality promotion. No critic Adam moments, repeated J1 weights, expanded coordinate archives or per-step feature caches. Recovery is exact at durable checkpoints; sudden interruption may lose progress since the last checkpoint (at most250updates or about30minutes normally), never falsely claim unsaved progress was recovered.

Measured warm forward-only decision times **{min(forward)*1000:.1f}–{max(forward)*1000:.1f}ms** for real selected prefixes90–398; measured peakGPU allocated{gpu['peak_allocated_bytes']/2**20:.1f}MiB, reserved{gpu['peak_reserved_bytes']/2**20:.1f}MiB, without optimizer/backward activations. Prior actual research forward/backward fixtures give{min(oldbw)*1000:.1f}–{max(oldbw)*1000:.1f}ms/decision. Extrapolating104 independent decisions gives **{resource['estimated_update_seconds'][0]:.1f}–{resource['estimated_update_seconds'][1]:.1f}s/update**, roughly **{resource['estimated_10000_update_hours'][0]:.1f}–{resource['estimated_10000_update_hours'][1]:.1f}hours for10k**, plus approximately0.5–2.5hours validation/generation/I/O overhead. These are projections, not measured long-run throughput; random coordinate access and power/thermal behavior can change them. No optimizer step was taken to refine this estimate. Peak hostRSS preflight{tests['host_peak_RSS_bytes']/gib:.2f}GiB. Full prior research optimizer/backward peak~1.1GiB is retained as supporting engineering evidence, not this task's forward-only peak.

Scientific limitations:goal supervision is local one-step/native-prefix imitation, not proven long-horizon reachability; explicit motifs can be copied; untrained encoder gradients are zero on the initial zero-residual update; native-validity envelope has limited original length calibration; balanced small panels have wide uncertainty; geometry-free best-AA retention may disagree with goal success. No claimed protein-quality gain or validated10k learning outcome exists yet. Next action is review and explicit source/config-bound training approval, then the single sealed supervised actor lineage only.

Exact dry-run and later launch commands: [LAUNCH_COMMANDS.md](LAUNCH_COMMANDS.md). No approval receipt is supplied and the launch is blocked without it.
''')
